# The chart-to-image contract (gonk-xsk3). Every invocation of a first-party gonk
# binary that the rendered chart makes, one per line:
#   <image> <argv0> [subcommand] [flag names, sorted]
# Flag VALUES are not part of the contract; flag SPELLING is.
#
# internal/buildgate (TestTheChartImageContractMatchesTheGoldensAndTheFloors)
# holds this file equal to what internal/charttest/testdata/golden invokes, and
# fails when an image's lines differ from origin/main unless that image's floor
# (chart/gonk/Chart.yaml gonk-factory.github.io/image-floor.<image>) went UP. A floor
# that goes DOWN always fails: floors only climb, because lowering one re-arms
# exactly the render G23 refuses today.
#
# Adding a line means the chart needs something the image may not have yet:
# land the binary first, confirm its tag exists (hack/require_image_tags.py),
# then raise the floor in the same change as this line.
#
# Binaries must keep accepting everything the previously released chart invokes
# for at least one chart release (expand/contract, gonk-4cox). This is policy,
# not a gate: see docs/plans/2026-09-13-chart-image-floor.md.
controller /usr/local/bin/gonk-gate sweep-health --max-age --supervisor-addr
controller gonk-gate capabilities
controller gonk-gate workstore-import
intake /usr/local/bin/gonk-intake
intake /usr/local/bin/gonk-intake netpol-probe -allow -deny -deny-l3 -dial-timeout -settle-timeout
meter /usr/local/bin/gonk-meter --listen --operator-config
